# Everything the build does not need. Two reasons this matters more than it looks: the whole context
# is sent to the daemon before the build starts, and a stale bin/ or obj/ from a host build can be
# copied over the container's own output and produce a binary nobody can account for.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/coverage/
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.idea/
.env
*.user
docs/
scripts/
